{
  "summary": "Fixes a bug where upgrading an existing temporary coin lock to a persistent lock does not update the in-memory persistence flag. In `CWallet::LoadLockedCoin`, the in-memory map entry is now updated when the coin is already present. This ensures that when the coin is subsequently spent, the persistent database record is properly erased instead of being resurrected on wallet restart.",
  "problem": "When a wallet user upgrades a non-persistent coin lock to a persistent lock, `std::map::emplace` does not overwrite the existing in-memory entry, leaving it marked as non-persistent. When that coin is subsequently spent, `UnlockCoin` assumes the lock was only temporary and skips deleting the persistent database record (`LOCKED_UTXO`), causing the spent coin to reappear as locked after restarting the wallet.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes issue #36304: 'wallet: upgrading a non-persistent coin lock to persistent leaves a stale lock on the spent output after restart'",
    "PR description explains the exact failure mode: 'Because emplace() was used without modifying the existing entry, the lock remained marked as temporary in memory. This caused subsequent spends to skip removing the persistent database record.'"
